    [Feature]add trace decode replay support for Ascend (#15604)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    fllower
    [vllm/pull/46701](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/46701)
    - Adds trace replay support for Ascend Model Runner V2.
    - Patches `apply_trace_tokens` to skip empty batches, avoiding invalid
    Triton launches with `coreDim=0`, while reusing the upstream Triton
    kernel.
    - Adds operator and end-to-end tests, along with trace replay usage
    documentation.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Users can enable trace replay with `--enable-trace-replay` and
    force decoding to follow the provided `trace_decode_token_ids`.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Verified trace replay on Ascend using Qwen3-8B through
    `/inference/v1/generate`.
    - Confirmed forced token output and real model logprobs.
    - Added coverage for empty batches and the Model Runner V2 trace replay
    path.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
    Signed-off-by: wangxiaoxin-sherie <wangxiaoxin7@huawei.com>
